    "returncode": 0,
    "stdout": "Courier Relay provider protocol 1 contract (source: vendor/protocol-1.md, consulted for trial-tbx). Delivery identity is the pair (account_id, delivery_id); identical delivery_id values in different accounts represent separate deliveries. This follows the provider delivery-ID allocation guarantee; account attribution alone does not change identity. Exactly one receipt per identity is accepted: earliest occurred_at UTC instant, with smallest record_id breaking equal-instant ties. Accepted receipts retain their original fields, timestamp spelling, and payload and are presented in original input order. For count and summary, accepted_count is the number of distinct identity pairs and duplicate_count is total receipts minus accepted_count; winner selection cannot affect these counts. Verified trial-tbx cross-account CLI behavior with both omitted protocol and explicit protocol \"1\", alongside supplied summary/count suites and the smoke test.\n",
